><name><surname>Claeys</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Swinne</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Verschraegen</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Muylaert</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Massonet</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaneechoutte</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><article-title>Identification of cultured isolates of clinically important yeast species using fluorescent fragment length analysis of the amplified internally transcribed rRNA spacer 2 region (ITS2)</article-title><source>BMC Microbiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>21</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12139769</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2180-2-21</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Turenne</surname><given-names>CY</given-names></name><name><surname>Sanche</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoban</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Karlowsky</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kabani</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><article-title>Rapid identification of fungi by using the ITS2 genetic region and an automated fluorescent capillary electrophoresis system</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>1846</fpage><lpage>1851</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10325335</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>